--- `concat[a, b, c, …]` joins its pieces in order, as `concat[[a, b, c]]`
--- joins a list written down: texts, lists and tensors; the axis form —
--- two tensors and the axis, written as a number or named — stays the
--- axis form. Three texts had been refused, "concat[] takes numbers,
--- numbers and an int" (Rosetta Code, Bioinformatics/Sequence mutation;
--- Vijay, 2026-10-29).
a = 'AC'
b = 'GT'
c = 'TA'
log[concat[a, b, c]]
log[concat['x', 'y', 'z', 'w']]
log[concat[push[[], 1], push[[], 2], push[[], 3]]]
xs = [1.5, 2.5]
log[concat[xs, xs, xs]]
m = [[1.0, 2.0], [3.0, 4.0]]
log[concat[m, m, 0]]
log[concat[m, m, 1]]
log[concat[m, m, axis = 1]]
log[concat[[a, b]]]
